<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M1, AC1.5: a masterLaneId that does not name a MASTER-roled
  track is REFUSED and announced, never adopted.

  THE FIXTURE IS THE POINT, and it is not hypothetical. Serialization in this
  tree is regenerated from live objects and there is no unknown-attribute
  passthrough, so an OLDER build opening a project written by this one drops
  systemRole= (it does not know it) while writing everything else back. The
  committed fixture is exactly that: master_lane.qxp with systemRole='master'
  stripped from the lane and masterLaneId= left pointing at it.

  Adopting that track would hand the user a master lane that answers
  systemRole() == None, and therefore one that accepts clips, can be armed,
  and would be summed as an ordinary track the moment M2 routes the sum
  through it. Keeping the constructor's own fresh lane is the safe answer.

  What the fresh lane must NOT have is the file's state: the fixture's lane
  carries one insert and a −6 dB fader, so plugins="0" volume="0" below is
  what separates "refused" from "adopted anyway".

  The role-lost track survives the load as an orphan referenced by nothing,
  which is the same thing that happens to any object no link names. It is not
  addressable and not audible; nothing here asserts it away.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="master_lane_bad_reference">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../master_lane_role_lost.qxp"/>

    <!-- It is announced, not silent. assert-log examines only the window
         since the action it FOLLOWS, so this has to sit directly under the
         load rather than at the end of the case. -->
    <assert-log contains="systemRole is not master" minCount="1"/>

    <!-- The user tracks loaded normally: the refusal is scoped to the master
         reference and takes nothing else down with it. -->
    <assert-track-count arrangement="" count="2"/>

    <!-- A master lane exists, and it is the CONSTRUCTOR's, not the file's. -->
    <assert-system-lane trackPath="$master" role="master" hidden="1"
                        acceptsClips="0" name="Master"
                        expectPath="$master" inChildLinks="0"
                        plugins="0" volume="0.0"/>

  </actions>

</SActionScript>
